{
	"_comment": "Who each character is, as a stack of LPC layers. Paths are relative to art-source/lpc/spritesheets. {anim} is the animation sheet (walk), {mood} the facial expression, {head} the head type for that character. Layers draw in the order listed, so hair goes last.",
	"_licensing": "Every layer here is licence-clean for a commercial release: its CREDITS.csv entry offers CC0, OGA-BY or CC-BY, so we elect one of those and avoid CC-BY-SA's share-alike and anti-DRM terms. build_characters.py re-checks this on every run and shouts if a layer is not clean. Do not add a layer without running it.",
	"_colours": "LPC ships every sheet in one reference palette and the web generator recolours it. We do the same offline: 'palette' names the ramp family, 'color' the target ramp, from art-source/lpc/palette_definitions/<family>/<family>_ulpc.json. null/null keeps a sheet as shipped.",
	"source": {
		"sheets": "lpc/spritesheets",
		"palettes": "lpc/palette_definitions",
		"credits": "lpc/CREDITS.csv"
	},
	"frame": 64,
	"walk_frames": 9,
	"walk_rows": {
		"up": 0,
		"left": 1,
		"down": 2,
		"right": 3
	},
	"sprite_scale": 2,
	"portrait_scale": 8,
	"portrait_size": [
		420,
		620
	],
	"_moods": "Maps the @mood tags writers use in .dlg files onto LPC facial expressions. An unlisted mood falls back to whatever 'default' points at.",
	"moods": {
		"default": "neutral",
		"tired": "sad",
		"worried": "sad",
		"wary": "anger",
		"tense": "anger",
		"cold": "anger",
		"angry": "anger",
		"amused": "happy",
		"flat": "neutral",
		"quiet": "neutral"
	},
